WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.870
[VEGAPUNK] I fear
that the world will not accept

3
00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:13.050
her, but she is a part
of it, all the same.

4
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.050
A true human
like anyone else.

5
00:00:16.780 --> 00:00:18.670
It was a success.

6
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.740
This is the first step.

7
00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:25.430
I'm confident that this will bring
peace to this planet someday.

8
00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:31.270
Signed, Dr. Vegapunk, Director
of mads, the Laboratory for Peace.

9
00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:11.940
<b>The Weight of Memory</b>

10
00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.720
We're all set to take
out the Vegapunks.

11
00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:11.740
We've got them
trapped like rats.

12
00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:15.900
Now then, how do we drag
the rats from their nest?

13
00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:16.680
That fool!

14
00:02:16.730 --> 00:02:18.830
The Frontier Dome won't
be easy to breach.

15
00:02:18.850 --> 00:02:20.370
Yeah, tell me about it.

16
00:02:21.580 --> 00:02:25.290
You know the Navy's rules about
attacking Emperors, don't you?

17
00:02:26.410 --> 00:02:29.540
I don't acknowledge
Straw Hat as an Emperor.

18
00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:32.760
Suit yourself, then.

19
00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:39.080
They move quickly.

20
00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.290
All of the sailing
routes are blocked.

21
00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:44.550
They've likely seized every
ship on the island by now.

22
00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:49.200
We still have Vegaforce-01,
but it can't operate beyond Egghead.

23
00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:52.370
They've turned our lab
into a kill zone.

24
00:02:55.220 --> 00:02:56.380
What will do the killing?

25
00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:57.950
Time to avenge Atlas, gang!

26
00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:01.750
Our objective right now is
to escape, not to engage them.

27
00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:05.280
But even so, a battle
may be inevitable.

28
00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:06.190
What's that?

29
00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:08.080
I wasn't listening.

30
00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:09.600
I gave myself chills.

31
00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:13.770
Oh, hey, Lilith, buddy, I don't think
they can even get up here right now.

32
00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:18.060
So let's just put a pin in the whole
killing idea and cool our collective jets.

33
00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:18.940
Yeah?

34
00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:20.090
Enough, Lilith.

35
00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.310
Charging in blindly will only
make things worse.

36
00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:26.310
Did you lose your spine
or something?

37
00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:29.640
These buttwipes are trying to take us out
and you don't even want to fight back?

38
00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:30.810
What's your deal?

39
00:03:31.690 --> 00:03:33.870
You are losing
sight of our goal.

40
00:03:34.250 --> 00:03:36.720
We need to get Stella
safely off the island.

41
00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:39.540
We're not getting anywhere
with the whole armada in the way.

42
00:03:39.540 --> 00:03:40.750
No, no.

43
00:03:40.830 --> 00:03:42.600
Everyone just settle
down, please.

44
00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:44.410
We are Stella's satellites.

45
00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:48.350
Our duty is to ensure his safety,
even at our own peril.

46
00:03:48.730 --> 00:03:51.080
We need to keep
our priorities straight.

47
00:03:51.720 --> 00:03:54.540
You running wild
won't help anything.

48
00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.850
This Goody shit is
going to get you killed.

49
00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:02.080
And I won't miss you.

50
00:04:02.160 --> 00:04:02.960
Just saying.

51
00:04:03.330 --> 00:04:04.160
Yes.

52
00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.040
Noted.

53
00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:09.810
Eureka!

54
00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:11.950
I just thought
of another invention!

55
00:04:12.030 --> 00:04:12.820
What can I...

56
00:04:12.820 --> 00:04:13.620
Look!

57
00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:15.100
Look!

58
00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:19.400
I don't have enough time or resources
or manpower to conduct the research!

59
00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:21.390
Where's my assistant cat?

60
00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:23.460
Oh, you were right there.

61
00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.310
That's meowsick
to my ears, Joshu!

62
00:04:26.390 --> 00:04:28.230
Oh, poor Sentomaru.

63
00:04:28.310 --> 00:04:31.140
You took my side
and ended up like this.

64
00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:32.240
I'm sorry.

65
00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:33.650
[PYTHAGORAS]
What should we do?

66
00:04:33.730 --> 00:04:37.690
There is one other person on this island
who we could call for help.

67
00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:38.560
[EDISON]
No, no, no, no, no, no!

68
00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:40.410
We can't just expose
our friend like that,

69
00:04:40.410 --> 00:04:42.050
The Government
would start a manhunt!

70
00:04:42.050 --> 00:04:44.300
We need to punk up
and handle this ourselves!

71
00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.160
[PYTHAGORAS]
I suppose you're right.

72
00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:48.420
[VEGAPUNK]
Anyway, that's the situation.

73
00:04:48.810 --> 00:04:51.270
I can't leave because
I'm stuck in the lab.

74
00:04:51.350 --> 00:04:52.650
Hold on, no!

75
00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:54.840
Making that call is
a death sentence!

76
00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:55.750
Stop!

77
00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:00.490
Now that you know the stakes,
I re-quasar your help out of this mess.

78
00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:01.540
[PYTHAGORAS, EDISON]
How could you?

79
00:05:01.540 --> 00:05:03.090
Have you no shame?

80
00:05:03.170 --> 00:05:04.460
[VOICE] Of course, Doctor.

81
00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.700
I expected your call
and I'm on the move.

82
00:05:06.700 --> 00:05:09.920
Did you hear that, everyone?

83
00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:11.920
Help is on the way!

84
00:05:13.510 --> 00:05:15.860
Well, I guess we are
in a bit of a pickle.

85
00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.830
Looks like we have no choice.

86
00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:22.390
I don't feel great about this, but we need
someone to handle CP0 so we can escape.

87
00:05:22.470 --> 00:05:23.430
Come on, guys.

88
00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:25.260
Let's get Stella on that ship.

89
00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:26.470
Works for me.

90
00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:29.900
Then I'll take Vegaforce-01 and carry
the ship to one of the ports.

91
00:05:29.940 --> 00:05:30.640
Good.

92
00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:31.810
Hurry and get it done.

93
00:05:31.890 --> 00:05:33.930
What the hell is
wrong with you?

94
00:05:34.010 --> 00:05:36.600
You just can't resist bossing
everyone around, huh?

95
00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:37.890
We're wasting time.

96
00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:39.520
Let's begin
the escape at once.

97
00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:40.720
You're doing it again!

98
00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:44.670
Alright.

99
00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.230
Seems we've got a plan.

100
00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.260
Passage on your ship.

101
00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.110
I assume there's
enough space.

102
00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:50.970
You know it.

103
00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:51.750
Let's go!

104
00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.770
That is to say,
I request-quasar room for seven.

105
00:05:54.850 --> 00:05:55.970
For seven?

106
00:05:56.050 --> 00:05:56.920
Ah, sweet!

107
00:05:57.000 --> 00:05:58.790
The other Vegapunks
are coming too?

108
00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:02.440
Seven of the world's best
scientists on my ship!

109
00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:03.220
Super!

110
00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:06.180
Are you kidding me?

111
00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:08.820
This deal keeps getting
worse and worse.

112
00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:11.150
All of the Vegapunks
are coming with us?

113
00:06:11.230 --> 00:06:13.130
So then that means...

114
00:06:13.210 --> 00:06:15.270
We get another
lady on the ship?

115
00:06:16.350 --> 00:06:18.360
Welcome to the team, Lilith!

116
00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:20.820
I'm so happy
to have you with us!

117
00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:26.170
Vegapunk!

118
00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:30.700
I'm gonna squish
you like a bug!

119
00:06:31.340 --> 00:06:32.250
What a mess!

120
00:06:32.330 --> 00:06:33.500
She forgot why she was mad!

121
00:06:33.500 --> 00:06:35.650
All she can think about
now are those bugs!

122
00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:36.500
Bonney!

123
00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.820
Please don't kick Mr.
Appleman's ass!

124
00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:39.940
I said I'd help him escape!

125
00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:40.430
Hey!

126
00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:42.200
Can you at least
wait till later?

127
00:06:42.280 --> 00:06:42.840
No!

128
00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:44.030
He's dead!

129
00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.630
Well, that sounds bad.

130
00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:55.130
Frontier Dome
now deactivated.

131
00:06:59.450 --> 00:07:00.280
What?

132
00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:02.210
Who could have done this?

133
00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:03.530
And for what purpose?

134
00:07:04.050 --> 00:07:05.350
Talk to me, Pythagoras!

135
00:07:05.430 --> 00:07:06.370
What's going on?

136
00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.030
I don't know!

137
00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:11.100
The interception protocol was
lifted without any warning!

138
00:07:11.180 --> 00:07:12.340
We're wide open!

139
00:07:12.420 --> 00:07:15.860
If the enemy heads for the Labophase
now, we can't stop them!

140
00:07:15.940 --> 00:07:16.530
Dammit!

141
00:07:16.530 --> 00:07:17.500
Check the control room!

142
00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:18.540
Is anyone in there?

143
00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:20.980
Control room?

144
00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:21.990
It's empty!

145
00:07:22.070 --> 00:07:26.070
I don't know how, but it seems
the barrier was deactivated remotely!

146
00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:29.540
Who could have pulled
off a stunt like that?

147
00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:37.020
Frontier Dome has
been deactivated!

148
00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:39.820
Did something
happen up there?

149
00:07:39.900 --> 00:07:40.970
Let's hurry!

150
00:07:41.050 --> 00:07:42.640
This is our chance, right?

151
00:07:42.720 --> 00:07:44.010
Who cares why?

152
00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:44.940
I do.

153
00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.350
Could be a trap.

154
00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:49.910
Or it could be
our only opening!

155
00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:52.420
We would be fools
to let it pass us by!

156
00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:54.780
This is entirely too convenient.

157
00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:56.690
I know we want in there.

158
00:07:57.080 --> 00:07:59.760
We can't complete
our mission if the barrier's up.

159
00:07:59.840 --> 00:08:02.700
Trap or not, this is
an improvement in my book.

160
00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:03.850
I'm going for it.

161
00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.190
You snooze, you lose!

162
00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:08.340
Well, there he goes.

163
00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:18.580
There!

164
00:08:18.580 --> 00:08:19.280
See that?

165
00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:20.340
Lemon squeezy!

166
00:08:20.420 --> 00:08:22.370
And nobody exploded,
what do you know?

167
00:08:22.450 --> 00:08:24.330
Well, it wasn't a trap.

168
00:08:24.410 --> 00:08:26.370
Let's bust the door
down and go get him!

169
00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:28.130
This is our golden opportunity!

170
00:08:28.630 --> 00:08:31.170
The wolves are
at your door, Vegapunk.

171
00:08:31.250 --> 00:08:34.500
Fortune has failed you
at the worst possible time.

172
00:08:37.520 --> 00:08:39.900
[STUSSY] Is that Straw Hat's
ship over there?

173
00:08:42.420 --> 00:08:43.590
[LUCCI] I see now.

174
00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:44.520
[chuckles]

175
00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:47.020
That's why it wasn't
on the coast when we arrived.

176
00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.710
A giant robot too?

177
00:08:48.790 --> 00:08:49.960
[LUCCI] It's an eyesore.

178
00:08:50.040 --> 00:08:50.970
Destroy it.

179
00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:53.330
I'll be done in a jiffy.

180
00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.410
[ZORO snores]

181
00:08:58.410 --> 00:08:59.930
And that takes
care of the dishes.

182
00:08:59.930 --> 00:09:03.890
Looks like I've still got plenty of time,
so I think I'll swab the deck next.

183
00:09:03.970 --> 00:09:08.150
I should probably look into that
ominous alarm, but, eh, I'm sure it's fine.

184
00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:13.800
[yells]

185
00:09:23.080 --> 00:09:24.020
Tempest Kick!

186
00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:26.230
Sky Slicer!

187
00:09:42.250 --> 00:09:47.770
What the hell?

188
00:09:46.400 --> 00:09:51.230
[alarm sounding]

189
00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.070
Zoro! What's going on?

190
00:09:49.150 --> 00:09:50.330
Are we under attack?! [STUSSY gasps]

191
00:09:53.780 --> 00:09:55.190
[growls] Who was that?

192
00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:57.870
Can't you see I was
trying to take a nap?

193
00:09:57.950 --> 00:09:59.100
Roronoa.

194
00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.000
[PYTHAGORAS] Shaka!

195
00:10:02.010 --> 00:10:02.710
Code Red!

196
00:10:02.750 --> 00:10:06.500
The Frontier Dome is up again,
but CP0 is already inside!

197
00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:09.620
[SHAKA]
Damn it. We're too late!

198
00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:12.980
[SHAKA] They're trying to destroy
the Straw Hats' ship.

199
00:10:13.060 --> 00:10:17.490
[PYTHAGORAS] Yes, but lucky for us a few
crew members stayed behind to protect it.

200
00:10:19.570 --> 00:10:21.240
[PYTHAGORAS]
We need to send backup!

201
00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:23.670
If we don't, we'll lose
our only escape!

202
00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:32.360
Oh well! Seems
violence is the answer.

203
00:10:32.440 --> 00:10:34.710
Now step back and leave
the feds to Killith.

204
00:10:34.790 --> 00:10:36.840
[SHAKA] And let you jeopardize
everyone's safety?

205
00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:37.990
Not a chance.

206
00:10:38.200 --> 00:10:40.070
[LILITH grunts]

207
00:10:42.590 --> 00:10:43.960
Bonney sure took off!

208
00:10:44.640 --> 00:10:45.790
Where'd she go?

209
00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.290
[gasps] Hey!

210
00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:49.800
We're here guys!

211
00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:51.760
Huh?

212
00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:53.550
Luffy!

213
00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:54.430
Chopper!

214
00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:58.860
[laughs]

215
00:10:57.850 --> 00:11:04.860
Oh man, you wouldn't believe
all the cool stuff we saw!

216
00:11:05.250 --> 00:11:06.430
Even found a robot!

217
00:11:06.510 --> 00:11:08.840
We agreed to take all
the Vegapunks with us.

218
00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:10.150
We'd better hurry up!

219
00:11:10.230 --> 00:11:12.850
Aww! But we just got here!

220
00:11:12.930 --> 00:11:14.880
We haven't even seen
the whole lab yet!

221
00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:16.970
Can't we stay a little longer?

222
00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:19.090
Maybe if you wanna
get murdered!

223
00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:22.200
Look, we'd love to stay,
but this is a Government Island!

224
00:11:22.280 --> 00:11:23.940
Also, Lucci is here!

225
00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:25.310
We hate that guy!

226
00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:29.740
What was that?

227
00:11:29.820 --> 00:11:31.100
It came from outside!

228
00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:33.450
[NAMI] Cipher Pol will show
up any second now.

229
00:11:33.530 --> 00:11:35.390
We'll get trapped
in another fight!

230
00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:37.610
Aw, come on.

231
00:11:37.690 --> 00:11:38.490
Oh!

232
00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:40.680
Have you guys seen Bonney?

233
00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:43.240
She's got long, pink hair,
and she's kinda mean.

234
00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:44.730
Bonney, huh?

235
00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:47.470
Is that the girl you were
hangin' with down in the city?

236
00:11:47.470 --> 00:11:48.650
Yeah, that's her.

237
00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:51.040
She's sorta tryin' to kill
Vegapunk right now.

238
00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:52.880
[ALL] What?

239
00:11:52.960 --> 00:11:54.330
Why would she do that?

240
00:11:54.410 --> 00:11:56.350
By the way, where is he?

241
00:11:56.810 --> 00:11:58.340
He was here a second ago!

242
00:12:01.150 --> 00:12:04.070
[screaming]

243
00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:04.960
[BONNEY] Die, Vegapunk!

244
00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:07.790
[screams]

245
00:12:07.820 --> 00:12:08.480
And he's dead!

246
00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:09.900
Oh, goddammit!

247
00:12:11.410 --> 00:12:12.590
Face me, you coward!

248
00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:18.300
Get back here!

249
00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.800
[VEGAPUNK] Stop it, Bonney!
I don't have time for this!

250
00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:25.250
Please, wait!

251
00:12:25.330 --> 00:12:29.340
I do want to speak with you, just
without the violence, if you don't mind!

252
00:12:29.340 --> 00:12:30.170
Go to hell!

253
00:12:31.580 --> 00:12:32.320
Bonney?

254
00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:33.230
Wahoo!

255
00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:35.390
Ahhh!

256
00:12:34.600 --> 00:12:36.310
[BONNEY yells]

257
00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:36.440
Ahh!

258
00:12:36.440 --> 00:12:38.520
I'm not letting
you go!

259
00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:44.530
You're gonna look me in the eye, and tell
me if you can turn back my father or not!

260
00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:46.740
Yes or no, live or die!

261
00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:48.940
[VEGAPUNK]
It's not that simple.

262
00:12:49.630 --> 00:12:50.750
I'm sorry.

263
00:12:50.830 --> 00:12:52.160
I can't.

264
00:12:52.620 --> 00:12:54.330
Then you've made
your choice!

265
00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:57.060
[growls]

266
00:12:57.060 --> 00:12:58.400
[gasps]

267
00:12:59.650 --> 00:13:02.940
[VEGAPUNK yells]

268
00:13:04.360 --> 00:13:05.790
This is for my father!

269
00:13:05.790 --> 00:13:09.920
I have a good reason,
I promise you!

270
00:13:14.430 --> 00:13:17.680
[yelping]

271
00:13:14.740 --> 00:13:15.540
Damn it!

272
00:13:15.440 --> 00:13:18.860
<b>Red Port

At the Foot
of the Red Line</b>

273
00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.250
Something fell from the wall!

274
00:14:23.950 --> 00:14:26.260
It's... Bartholomew Kuma!

275
00:14:26.740 --> 00:14:27.280
What?

276
00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:28.640
Where did he come from?

277
00:14:29.250 --> 00:14:33.100
Actually, I think I heard in the news
that he escaped from Mary Geoise.

278
00:14:33.180 --> 00:14:34.860
But why is he here?

279
00:14:34.940 --> 00:14:38.000
The Celestial Dragons called
him their invincible slave!

280
00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:39.220
He's huge!

281
00:14:56.530 --> 00:15:02.220
A former warlord of the sea,
Bartholomew Kuma, has appeared!

282
00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:06.010
He's currently in the northeast,
near the entrance of Moldoros!

283
00:15:08.190 --> 00:15:10.730
All marines,
dispatch immediately!

284
00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:21.100
All citizens, let's
evacuate the area!

285
00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:24.740
Do not approach Kuma
under any circumstance!

286
00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:27.180
He's property
of the Celestial Dragons!

287
00:15:27.550 --> 00:15:29.330
He no longer has
a human mind!

288
00:15:29.880 --> 00:15:31.920
His current programming
is unknown!

289
00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:36.500
Repeat, for your own safety,
all citizens must evacuate at once!

290
00:15:48.220 --> 00:15:50.320
[BONNEY] It hurts!

291
00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:53.500
I must have broken
my leg when I fell down!

292
00:15:54.070 --> 00:15:56.660
Oh. Oh, no.

293
00:15:58.720 --> 00:15:59.550
The poor girl!

294
00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:04.310
I'll go get help!
We need the med team!

295
00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:07.700
I'm sorry, Bonney!

296
00:16:13.380 --> 00:16:15.320
[BONNEY] Distorted Future!

297
00:16:19.050 --> 00:16:20.380
Now you die!

298
00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:23.580
[yells]

299
00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:25.500
[VEGAPUNK screams]

300
00:16:26.700 --> 00:16:29.020
I've been swindled!

301
00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:31.130
[growls]

302
00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:34.000
It's time to end this!

303
00:16:34.080 --> 00:16:36.520
[VEGAPUNK] Please, just listen!
Even if you kill me.

304
00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:37.920
Age!

305
00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:38.830
Skewer!

306
00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:54.290
[VEGAPUNK screams]

307
00:17:01.440 --> 00:17:02.360
No, sir.

308
00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:05.530
Why do I have to be a baby?

309
00:17:05.610 --> 00:17:07.050
And what are these gems?

310
00:17:07.410 --> 00:17:08.910
Oh! My golden years!

311
00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:10.770
Bonney!

312
00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:13.270
Give back the shining
years of my life!

313
00:17:16.860 --> 00:17:18.370
[BONNEY] Stop your whining!

314
00:17:18.450 --> 00:17:20.860
My powers don't work
on living things forever.

315
00:17:20.940 --> 00:17:23.400
It'll wear off, but not before
we're done here.

316
00:17:23.480 --> 00:17:24.900
Now out with it.

317
00:17:24.980 --> 00:17:27.020
What was your good reason?

318
00:17:29.340 --> 00:17:30.810
[BONNEY]
You said you had one.

319
00:17:31.380 --> 00:17:32.820
So spit it out!

320
00:17:32.900 --> 00:17:34.700
Why did you kill my father?

321
00:17:36.570 --> 00:17:39.700
[VEGAPUNK] If I tell you, it will only
bring you more pain.

322
00:17:40.170 --> 00:17:41.020
I'm sorry.

323
00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:43.520
I want to help, I truly do.

324
00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:44.430
But no.

325
00:17:45.070 --> 00:17:45.870
What?!

326
00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:50.680
[VEGAPUNK] I made a promise
with your father.

327
00:17:51.110 --> 00:17:52.000
You see.

328
00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:59.730
<b>Red Port</b>

329
00:17:56.620 --> 00:17:57.740
[RED PORT CITIZEN A]
Look, it's Kuma!

330
00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:59.820
He's climbing straight
up the Red Line!

331
00:17:59.900 --> 00:18:02.810
[RED PORT CITIZEN B] Surely they're gonna
stop him before he dies.

332
00:18:02.890 --> 00:18:04.520
Before he gets to the top!

333
00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:12.980
[VEGAPUNK]
Before he lost his humanity,

334
00:18:12.980 --> 00:18:16.810
I swore to him that I'd never
tell you why it happened.

335
00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:26.730
[BONNEY] You had a reason to kill my father,
but you can't say it?

336
00:18:26.810 --> 00:18:27.450
Screw you!

337
00:18:27.450 --> 00:18:30.150
Who would believe that crap?

338
00:18:30.490 --> 00:18:32.080
Do you think I'm stupid?

339
00:18:32.160 --> 00:18:33.600
Of course I don't!

340
00:18:33.680 --> 00:18:34.560
It's the truth!

341
00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:37.320
So please let me go!

342
00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:39.360
[growls]

343
00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:42.660
Kuma chose to give up
his humanity on his own.

344
00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:44.260
It wasn't me!

345
00:18:44.340 --> 00:18:46.850
It was his choice,
and no one else's!

346
00:18:46.930 --> 00:18:47.730
[BONNEY] You're lying!

347
00:18:48.850 --> 00:18:50.540
You're saying he
chose this hell?

348
00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:52.550
That he chose
to abandon me?

349
00:18:53.250 --> 00:18:54.830
You killed him!

350
00:18:55.190 --> 00:18:57.600
It was hell for me as well.

351
00:18:57.680 --> 00:18:59.690
I can't even stand
to remember it!

352
00:19:16.160 --> 00:19:18.790
[VEGAPUNK] Your father is
an extraordinary man!

353
00:19:19.180 --> 00:19:21.220
I'm proud to call
him my friend!

354
00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:23.320
I truly care for him!

355
00:19:23.400 --> 00:19:24.780
I swear to you!

356
00:19:24.860 --> 00:19:28.780
And that is exactly why
I won't breathe a word!

357
00:19:29.430 --> 00:19:30.590
You bastard!

358
00:19:34.580 --> 00:19:36.920
I'm sick of your
self-serving lies!

359
00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.820
I'm not gonna
let you trick me!

360
00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:40.540
[screams]

361
00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:41.660
This is abuse!

362
00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:43.610
I can't take it!

363
00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.380
[gasps]

364
00:19:47.590 --> 00:19:53.600
[beeping]

365
00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:54.020
It's just a broken
contraption, Bonney!

366
00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:57.360
It has nothing to do
with Kuma, I promise!

367
00:19:57.780 --> 00:19:59.130
Lying again.

368
00:20:02.700 --> 00:20:04.180
Oiled Shock.

369
00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:22.320
Stupid Bonney!

370
00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:37.550
You're wrong.

371
00:20:42.640 --> 00:20:43.840
Please, no!

372
00:20:52.650 --> 00:20:54.320
A person's thoughts?

373
00:20:54.400 --> 00:20:55.510
[VEGAPUNK] Indeed.

374
00:20:55.590 --> 00:21:00.260
There was a scholar in the West Blue
who made a revolutionary discovery.

375
00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:04.880
They said people lose 21 grams
of weight at the moment of death.

376
00:21:05.480 --> 00:21:08.850
So, you might say
that's the weight of a human soul.

377
00:21:08.850 --> 00:21:09.680
Oh!

378
00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:16.350
Of course, there's much more testing to do,
but I think it's proof that the soul exists.

379
00:21:16.430 --> 00:21:18.420
In fact, I'm certain of it!

380
00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:21.880
[KUMA] Hmm.

381
00:21:21.880 --> 00:21:24.010
I'm afraid this one
might be beyond me.

382
00:21:25.030 --> 00:21:26.030
Hmm.

383
00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:28.290
On the contrary,
you're an expert!

384
00:21:29.260 --> 00:21:31.270
It is similar to your power.

385
00:21:35.500 --> 00:21:38.660
A person's pain is
intangible, yes?

386
00:21:38.740 --> 00:21:43.460
But you can take it from their body
and transfer it to someone else!

387
00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:51.680
Nerves create electrical signals, and you
can move them without using wires.

388
00:21:56.560 --> 00:21:59.800
[VEGAPUNK] Ah. Let's compare it
to mental images instead.

389
00:22:00.210 --> 00:22:01.570
Mental images?

390
00:22:01.650 --> 00:22:02.320
[VEGAPUNK] Yes.

391
00:22:02.320 --> 00:22:07.750
Memories and other images you see in your
minds-eye are also signals from nerve cells.

392
00:22:09.910 --> 00:22:11.600
How much do they weigh?

393
00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:13.200
How big are they?

394
00:22:13.280 --> 00:22:15.350
That's what I want to know!

395
00:22:15.430 --> 00:22:16.860
Fascinating, isn't it?

396
00:22:15.650 --> 00:22:17.570
[sighs]

397
00:22:17.570 --> 00:22:20.770
You want me to take out
my memories and show them to you?

398
00:22:20.850 --> 00:22:22.850
Are you trying
to humiliate me?

399
00:22:22.930 --> 00:22:24.430
[VEGAPUNK] I'm begging you!

400
00:22:24.510 --> 00:22:26.110
Do it for the sake of science!

401
00:22:26.190 --> 00:22:28.040
I won't show them to anyone!

402
00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:29.560
Pretty please?

403
00:22:29.640 --> 00:22:30.610
Forget it!

404
00:22:30.690 --> 00:22:33.500
I could never trust you
with something as sensitive as that!

405
00:22:33.460 --> 00:22:35.300
[yells]

406
00:22:33.500 --> 00:22:34.550
Ah!

407
00:22:35.350 --> 00:22:36.510
Oh, come now!

408
00:22:36.590 --> 00:22:38.570
I must know!

409
00:22:38.650 --> 00:22:39.570
Stop it!

410
00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:41.310
You must not touch that paw!

411
00:22:41.390 --> 00:22:43.520
It is suffering given form!

412
00:22:44.200 --> 00:22:45.280
You could die!

413
00:22:45.360 --> 00:22:47.070
You know Kuma's power!

414
00:22:47.660 --> 00:22:50.140
The pain he amasses
is unbearable!

415
00:22:50.220 --> 00:22:51.860
It will kill you!

416
00:22:53.260 --> 00:22:54.100
You're wrong.

417
00:22:54.620 --> 00:22:55.650
It's not pain.

418
00:22:57.570 --> 00:22:58.380
Dad...

419
00:23:04.110 --> 00:23:07.120
<b>Red Port</b>

420
00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:10.310
Shoot Kuma down on sight!

421
00:23:10.390 --> 00:23:12.110
He cannot reach Marie's wall!

422
00:23:17.340 --> 00:23:18.140
Oh!

423
00:23:20.480 --> 00:23:21.280
Ugh...

424
00:23:22.370 --> 00:23:23.280
Light him up!

425
00:23:25.060 --> 00:23:25.890
Ugh...

426
00:23:28.410 --> 00:23:29.690
[MARINE A]
Alright, he's down!

427
00:23:35.240 --> 00:23:35.920
Hurry!

428
00:23:35.920 --> 00:23:36.760
Surround him!

429
00:23:42.970 --> 00:23:44.010
[MARINE B]
Evacuate the area!

430
00:23:44.090 --> 00:23:44.960
It's dangerous!

431
00:23:45.040 --> 00:23:46.240
[RED PORT CITIZEN A]
Everybody run, everyone!

432
00:23:46.340 --> 00:23:48.160
You'll get caught
in the attack?

433
00:23:56.870 --> 00:23:59.180
I know my father's power.

434
00:23:59.260 --> 00:23:59.960
What?

435
00:24:01.230 --> 00:24:03.710
So I know what I'm seeing...

436
00:24:04.430 --> 00:24:05.590
And it isn't pain.

437
00:24:05.670 --> 00:24:06.950
Finish him off!

438
00:24:09.250 --> 00:24:10.350
[MARINE OFFICER A]
Pull back!

439
00:24:10.680 --> 00:24:12.720
[MARINES scream]

440
00:24:10.990 --> 00:24:11.820
The...

441
00:24:16.210 --> 00:24:17.260
Truth is...

442
00:24:20.010 --> 00:24:21.660
These are his memories.

443
00:24:51.040 --> 00:24:52.500
[giggles]

444
00:24:51.430 --> 00:24:54.810
<b>Lab</b>

445
00:24:51.790 --> 00:24:52.490
What?

446
00:24:52.500 --> 00:24:54.700
How did Lucci get
up here so fast?

447
00:24:54.780 --> 00:24:57.680
[SHAKA] Unfortunately, it seems there
was a glitch in the system.

448
00:24:57.760 --> 00:24:59.660
At least the Sunny
will still be okay!

449
00:24:59.740 --> 00:25:01.750
There's no way they'll
beat Zoro and Brook!

450
00:25:01.750 --> 00:25:03.180
It's two against three.

451
00:25:03.260 --> 00:25:04.970
I wouldn't be so sure just yet.

452
00:25:06.420 --> 00:25:07.900
[SHAKA]
No, look at the monitor.

453
00:25:08.400 --> 00:25:11.170
I'm afraid their odds are
much worse than that.

454
00:25:10.780 --> 00:25:12.110
[gasps]

455
00:25:11.710 --> 00:25:12.670
[USOPP] No way!

456
00:25:13.300 --> 00:25:14.860
The seraphim are here, too?

457
00:25:15.600 --> 00:25:19.090
[SHAKA] It's two of your crewmates
against seven killing machines.

458
00:25:19.540 --> 00:25:22.130
We didn't order them
to come up here.

459
00:25:22.530 --> 00:25:24.470
[STUSSY] They're stuck
with us, either way.

460
00:25:25.630 --> 00:25:28.040
The Dome closed right
after they came in.

461
00:25:29.990 --> 00:25:31.340
Oh, c'mon!

462
00:25:31.420 --> 00:25:33.910
They snuck the seraphim
in while the Dome was down.

463
00:25:33.910 --> 00:25:34.640
No fair!

464
00:25:34.720 --> 00:25:38.730
[SHAKA] Actually, I don't think CP0
intended to bring them here at all.

465
00:25:38.810 --> 00:25:39.610
Say what?

466
00:25:40.730 --> 00:25:42.550
[SHAKA]
It's a feature of the seraphim.

467
00:25:43.240 --> 00:25:47.120
In some circumstances, they
can make basic decisions on their own.

468
00:25:48.970 --> 00:25:52.140
They must've figured out that the Dome
would be back soon and made a move.

469
00:25:52.140 --> 00:25:52.930
[SHAKA] Yes.

470
00:25:53.010 --> 00:25:54.550
But this could work
on its own.

471
00:25:54.550 --> 00:25:58.210
If the seraphim are in our favor,
we can turn this battle around.

472
00:25:58.870 --> 00:26:00.230
How would we do that?

473
00:26:00.690 --> 00:26:03.510
They've got us backed
into a corner, don't they?

474
00:26:04.170 --> 00:26:07.050
<b>Authority Chip
 (CP0)</b>

475
00:26:04.170 --> 00:26:07.090
<b>Sentomaru</b>

476
00:26:04.170 --> 00:26:10.130
<b>The Five Elders</b>
<b>Vegapunk</b>

477
00:26:05.610 --> 00:26:10.050
[SHAKA] Our orders outrank CP0's
on the seraphim's scale of authority.

478
00:26:10.130 --> 00:26:13.120
Once we reach them,
they'll answer to us.

479
00:26:14.070 --> 00:26:14.870
Heh, heh.

480
00:26:21.100 --> 00:26:24.100
<b>Labophase
Egghead</b>

481
00:26:21.590 --> 00:26:22.390
Get out.

482
00:26:23.740 --> 00:26:24.570
Huh?

483
00:26:25.310 --> 00:26:26.140
Shit!

484
00:26:31.220 --> 00:26:32.830
[EDISON] Then we'd
better get over there

485
00:26:32.830 --> 00:26:35.330
and give them some orders
before it's too late!

486
00:26:35.410 --> 00:26:35.850
Hang on.

487
00:26:35.850 --> 00:26:37.200
I'm coming, Straw Hats!

488
00:26:38.970 --> 00:26:42.860
[gasps] Hey, wait for me!

489
00:26:40.730 --> 00:26:41.770
[LILITH giggles]

490
00:26:42.940 --> 00:26:44.910
[EDISON]
Are you taking this seriously?

491
00:26:44.990 --> 00:26:46.240
Of course I am!

492
00:26:46.320 --> 00:26:46.900
[EDISON] Good.

493
00:26:46.900 --> 00:26:48.900
Let's hope those
two can hold out.

494
00:26:49.410 --> 00:26:50.140
[SHAKA] Don't dawdle!

495
00:26:50.220 --> 00:26:51.520
We're counting on you two!

496
00:26:51.550 --> 00:26:52.270
Hey, no!

497
00:26:52.350 --> 00:26:53.150
Boss!

498
00:26:54.490 --> 00:26:55.440
Zoro!

499
00:26:55.520 --> 00:26:58.110
I've gotta hit you
with everything I've got!

500
00:26:59.390 --> 00:27:00.450
Oh, this is bad!

501
00:27:00.530 --> 00:27:03.590
Even Zoro and Brook can't
take on all of them at once!

502
00:27:03.670 --> 00:27:05.650
In that case,
I'll go back 'em up!

503
00:27:05.730 --> 00:27:07.150
[USOPP]
Good luck out there, pal!

504
00:27:07.230 --> 00:27:09.000
I'm just gonna hide in here.

505
00:27:09.080 --> 00:27:10.750
Uh, I mean, guard the base.

506
00:27:10.830 --> 00:27:13.490
Guess Mosshead won't live
to see the One Piece, huh?

507
00:27:13.570 --> 00:27:14.380
What a shame.

508
00:27:14.460 --> 00:27:16.140
Your crewmates
need you, you idiot!

509
00:27:16.140 --> 00:27:17.490
Get out there and help!

510
00:27:18.420 --> 00:27:21.100
Did my darling Nami
just give me an order?

511
00:27:21.180 --> 00:27:22.010
I'm on it!

512
00:27:22.990 --> 00:27:25.620
Consider me your own
personal seraphim!

513
00:27:25.040 --> 00:27:26.540
<b>HHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH
HHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH
HHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH Sanji-phim Rank of Authority</b>

514
00:27:25.040 --> 00:27:28.130
<b>The Ladies: Absolute Obedience</b>

515
00:27:25.700 --> 00:27:28.890
Sanji-phim is here to do
anything you ask him to!

516
00:27:26.540 --> 00:27:26.620
<b>HHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH
HHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH
HHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHHH</b>

517
00:27:26.620 --> 00:27:30.000
<b>The Guys: It Depends</b>

518
00:27:28.130 --> 00:27:28.920
<b>The Ladies: Absolute Obedience</b>

519
00:27:28.630 --> 00:27:30.000
<b>Moss Head</b>

520
00:27:29.580 --> 00:27:30.240
Wait.

521
00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:32.420
Why do I have
to save Mosshead?

522
00:27:32.500 --> 00:27:34.410
'Cause we need him,
Curly-phim.

523
00:27:34.910 --> 00:27:36.560
Now, c'mon, we've
gotta hurry!

524
00:27:42.980 --> 00:27:44.810
[KAKU] This is a lucky break.

525
00:27:45.170 --> 00:27:47.940
I've been waiting to settle
the score with you,

526
00:27:49.630 --> 00:27:51.280
Time for round two.

527
00:27:53.280 --> 00:27:54.080
Ready?

528
00:27:54.680 --> 00:27:55.740
Let's go.

529
00:27:57.210 --> 00:27:58.000
Hold on.

530
00:27:58.080 --> 00:27:59.990
I thought he was a giraffe.

531
00:28:00.070 --> 00:28:01.740
That's what he's
supposed to be,

532
00:28:01.820 --> 00:28:04.000
but I guess he does
look kinda weird.

533
00:28:04.630 --> 00:28:05.850
Well, whatever.

534
00:28:05.930 --> 00:28:08.340
He's gettin' cut
down, either way.

535
00:28:08.420 --> 00:28:10.580
[KAKU] You think it'll be
that easy, do you?

536
00:28:10.660 --> 00:28:11.920
Just try me!

537
00:28:12.810 --> 00:28:14.700
Look after the ship, okay?

538
00:28:14.780 --> 00:28:15.880
Roger that!

539
00:28:15.960 --> 00:28:17.160
You'd better not flinch!

540
00:28:17.720 --> 00:28:18.770
Nose Pistol!

541
00:28:20.510 --> 00:28:21.590
[gasps]

542
00:28:23.930 --> 00:28:25.340
That's just a sample!

543
00:28:25.420 --> 00:28:26.850
Here comes the main course!

544
00:28:26.930 --> 00:28:27.940
Giraffe Blast!

545
00:28:30.810 --> 00:28:33.320
[KAKU] Plenty more where
that came from!

546
00:28:45.840 --> 00:28:47.880
This isn't anything new to me.

547
00:28:48.220 --> 00:28:51.300
I fought a guy with a long neck in Wano,
too.

548
00:28:53.110 --> 00:28:55.600
Now get the hell
away from our ship!

549
00:29:12.800 --> 00:29:15.570
[LUCCI] We'll take out the lab
and Vegapunk with it.

550
00:29:15.650 --> 00:29:17.570
Destroy everything in sight!

551
00:29:35.580 --> 00:29:36.070
[SHAKA] No!

552
00:29:36.070 --> 00:29:38.190
The seraphim are
aiming for the lab!

553
00:29:57.540 --> 00:29:58.460
[JINBE] We're trapped!

554
00:29:58.890 --> 00:30:01.190
[SHAKA] If our allies fail,
we'll all be crushed!

555
00:30:01.270 --> 00:30:01.770
[NAMI] What?

556
00:30:01.770 --> 00:30:02.570
Crushed?

557
00:30:14.770 --> 00:30:18.020
[NAMI, USOPP scream]

558
00:30:24.290 --> 00:30:25.330
[gasps] Oh, no.

559
00:30:26.900 --> 00:30:31.060
[KAKU] Whether you defeat me or not,
there's no getting out of this alive.

560
00:30:31.140 --> 00:30:33.870
[KAKU] Really showboating today,
aren't you, kids?

561
00:30:34.420 --> 00:30:35.700
Those bastards!

562
00:30:44.560 --> 00:30:47.720
Keep this up, and we'll have
the mission done before lunch!

563
00:30:47.570 --> 00:30:50.490
[BOTH screaming]

564
00:30:47.800 --> 00:30:51.540
Ah!

565
00:30:53.590 --> 00:30:58.090
Ah!

566
00:30:56.090 --> 00:30:58.380
[laughs]

567
00:31:02.000 --> 00:31:03.920
[KAKU] Stussy, you...

568
00:31:04.000 --> 00:31:04.700
Uh...

569
00:31:05.090 --> 00:31:05.890
Uh-uh...

570
00:31:18.540 --> 00:31:19.370
Cuckoo!

571
00:31:22.940 --> 00:31:23.770
[LUCCI] Stussy!

572
00:31:24.320 --> 00:31:25.520
What are you doing?

573
00:31:26.630 --> 00:31:27.630
Answer me!

574
00:31:30.300 --> 00:31:31.420
Oh, nothing.

575
00:31:32.560 --> 00:31:34.640
Just putting a bad
boy to sleep.

576
00:31:39.000 --> 00:31:40.740
Do me a favor, Lucci.

577
00:31:42.220 --> 00:31:44.150
Why don't you join him?

578
00:31:45.970 --> 00:31:49.220
<b>Modeled After
Miss Buckingham Stussy
of the Rocks Pirates</b>
<b>Stussy
MADS Clone Experiment
First Successful Subject</b>

579
00:31:49.220 --> 00:31:53.140
<b>A Stretch of Sea
in the New World</b>

580
00:31:54.770 --> 00:31:56.770
[chuckles]

581
00:32:03.100 --> 00:32:05.440
[screams]

582
00:32:08.860 --> 00:32:11.350
That's gotta be the biggest
fish I've ever seen!

583
00:32:11.430 --> 00:32:14.500
They say there's something
unusual about these waters.

584
00:32:14.880 --> 00:32:16.490
This should be fun.

585
00:32:17.260 --> 00:32:18.500
Is that an island?

586
00:32:20.030 --> 00:32:21.160
[KILLER] Kid, wake up!

587
00:32:21.240 --> 00:32:22.070
[KID] Huh?

588
00:32:22.600 --> 00:32:24.280
[KILLER]
We've got land up ahead.

589
00:32:24.360 --> 00:32:25.650
Should we drop anchor?

590
00:32:26.170 --> 00:32:27.810
That's a dumb question.

591
00:32:28.300 --> 00:32:30.140
We've made it
this far, haven't we?

592
00:32:30.220 --> 00:32:32.660
So there's no island
left for us to fear.

593
00:32:33.110 --> 00:32:34.010
Hold up.

594
00:32:34.090 --> 00:32:34.940
Wait.

595
00:32:35.020 --> 00:32:36.500
The hell is that?

596
00:32:40.360 --> 00:32:42.360
[KILLER] I think I might
know where we are.

597
00:32:42.960 --> 00:32:44.860
It's the island
of the Giants... Elbaph!

598
00:32:45.350 --> 00:32:46.540
Elbaph.

599
00:32:49.120 --> 00:32:50.380
Interesting.

600
00:32:51.120 --> 00:32:53.370
<b>Marine Headquarters
G-14 Branch</b>

601
00:32:53.590 --> 00:32:54.960
Absolutely not.

602
00:32:55.040 --> 00:32:56.090
Are you kidding me?

603
00:32:56.540 --> 00:32:59.270
We're headed out for the Egghead
mission any minute now.

604
00:32:59.270 --> 00:33:02.160
I'm not gonna lend you
my troops at a time like this!

605
00:33:02.240 --> 00:33:05.470
[GARP] Are they too busy removing
that stick from your caboose?

606
00:33:05.020 --> 00:33:07.890
[laughs]

607
00:33:05.550 --> 00:33:07.070
Ha ha ha ha ha ha!

608
00:33:07.850 --> 00:33:09.450
[DOLL]
Laugh it up all you want.

609
00:33:09.530 --> 00:33:10.990
My answer's still no.

610
00:33:11.070 --> 00:33:13.810
Besides, that island's
an Emperor's turf!

611
00:33:13.890 --> 00:33:15.580
Did you get
clearance to invade?

612
00:33:15.660 --> 00:33:17.730
I bet the brass popped
a vein when you asked.

613
00:33:17.730 --> 00:33:19.860
[GARP] I have to ask?

614
00:33:19.940 --> 00:33:20.790
Huh?

615
00:33:20.870 --> 00:33:23.640
Come on, how many decades
have you been a Marine?

616
00:33:23.720 --> 00:33:25.030
Ha ha ha ha ha!

617
00:33:25.460 --> 00:33:27.010
[GARP] Eh, it'll all work out!

618
00:33:27.550 --> 00:33:28.930
I'm here, by the way.

619
00:33:29.010 --> 00:33:30.120
Wait, what?

620
00:33:32.280 --> 00:33:32.990
Helmeppo!

621
00:33:33.070 --> 00:33:33.900
Boo!

622
00:33:34.450 --> 00:33:35.220
Huh?

623
00:33:35.300 --> 00:33:36.650
Get yer butt out here!

624
00:33:37.050 --> 00:33:37.850
Huh?

625
00:33:39.090 --> 00:33:39.340
[HIBARI] What?

626
00:33:39.340 --> 00:33:40.090
Is it a pirate?

627
00:33:40.170 --> 00:33:42.820
It sounds like they've come here
to take revenge on Helmeppo!

628
00:33:42.820 --> 00:33:43.670
[MARINE A] No!

629
00:33:43.760 --> 00:33:44.560
Wait!

630
00:33:44.640 --> 00:33:45.340
Huh?

631
00:33:51.230 --> 00:33:52.030
[GARP] Oh, good!

632
00:33:52.380 --> 00:33:53.720
There you are, boy!

633
00:33:53.800 --> 00:33:55.630
Didn't keep me waiting!

634
00:33:55.710 --> 00:33:57.030
Vice Admiral Garp!

635
00:33:59.490 --> 00:34:01.290
I'm so glad you're here!

636
00:34:01.370 --> 00:34:04.440
Koby got caught
by Blackbeard.

637
00:34:05.350 --> 00:34:06.490
It wasn't his fault.

638
00:34:06.570 --> 00:34:07.690
He was so brave!

639
00:34:07.770 --> 00:34:09.110
But I was helpless!

640
00:34:09.460 --> 00:34:11.730
I couldn't do anything!

641
00:34:11.810 --> 00:34:14.260
Would you stop
your blubbering already?

642
00:34:14.340 --> 00:34:15.750
You look like a fool!

643
00:34:16.980 --> 00:34:20.280
We just wanna help him!

644
00:34:20.880 --> 00:34:22.030
[GARP] Glad to hear it!

645
00:34:22.110 --> 00:34:23.110
Hop aboard!

646
00:34:24.040 --> 00:34:25.350
Pirate Island?

647
00:34:25.430 --> 00:34:28.070
You think that'll scare off
an old Marine like me?

648
00:34:28.150 --> 00:34:30.810
We'll give those bastards
a beating on their own turf!

649
00:34:30.810 --> 00:34:33.320
We're gonna kick
down their front door!

650
00:34:33.400 --> 00:34:35.110
And rescue Koby!

651
00:34:35.490 --> 00:34:37.050
[BOTH] Vice Admiral Garp!

652
00:34:38.490 --> 00:34:42.790
[laughs]
